    "title": "Week 1: position 1, clean changes, triads and double stops",
    "summary": "A minor pentatonic position 1, G-C-D changes, and the same chords made smaller: power chords, triads and double stops. One idea a day, each drill says what it trains and why, and by day 7 you make up drills of your own.",
    "progress": "Techniques: the spider is clean from frets 5 and 1 at a slow tempo; double stops are new. Next: the spider in a new finger order, a little faster.\nBasic chords: G, C, D and Em change in time at 70 with down strums; the full strum pattern at 80 was only met on day 7. Next: keep the pattern, add a new chord.\nScales: A minor pentatonic position 1 from memory at 80, and phrases that end on the root. E minor in the open position is new. Next: position 2, and joining it to position 1.\nCAGED: G, C and D triads on the top strings and one set lower, slowly. Next: the same triads in a second place on the neck.",
